.TH HAWK 1 "July 2026" Linux "Hawk Manual"

.SH NAME
hawk \- Scheme (R7RS) JIT

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hawk
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIscript\fR [\fIarg\fR ...]]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hawk
is a virtual machine and just-in-time compiler for R7RS Scheme.
It runs a script directly from bytecode or loads an explicit image file.

The first non-option argument is treated as the script name.  Any remaining
arguments are passed through to the script.

.SH OPTIONS
.SS Normal options
.TP
.BI "\-o, \-\-joff"
Turn off the JIT compiler and only use the bytecode VM.
.TP
.BI "\-i, \-\-image " FILE
Load an explicit \fB.bc\fR image file instead of the default image.
.TP
.BI "\-D " NAME
Add \fINAME\fR to the Scheme feature list before loading a script.
May be specified more than once.
.TP
.BI "\-I " DIRECTORY
Prepend \fIDIRECTORY\fR to the Scheme library search path before loading a script.
May be specified more than once.
.TP
.BI "\-A " DIRECTORY
Append \fIDIRECTORY\fR to the Scheme library search path before loading a script.
May be specified more than once.
.TP
.BI "\-\-list"
Compile the script and list its bytecode without running it.
.TP
.BI "\-\-exe"
Generate an executable from the Scheme source file.
The output path is the script path with the trailing \fB.scm\fR suffix removed.
The generated executable links against \fBlibhawk_core\fR with the system
linker; install Hawk first or set normal compiler and loader search paths such
as \fBLIBRARY_PATH\fR and \fBLD_LIBRARY_PATH\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-profile"
Turn on the sampling profiler, showing VM, GC, and JIT time.
.TP
.BI "\-\-version"
Print the program version string and exit.
.TP
.BI "\-h, \-\-help"
Print the help text and exit.
.TP
.BI "\-v, \-\-verbose[=" CATEGORIES ]
Turn on verbose logging.  Without categories, all logging is enabled.
Categories are comma-separated and include
\fBgc\fR, \fBtrace\fR, \fBrecord\fR, \fBjit\fR, \fBregalloc\fR, \fBasm\fR,
and \fBir\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-unsafe
Disable array bounds checks.

.SS Debug options
.TP
.BI "\-m, \-\-max-trace " NUMBER
Stop JITting after \fINUMBER\fR traces and then interpret.
.TP
.BI "\-d, \-\-dump"
Dump Linux perf JIT information.
.TP
.BI "\-s " SEED
Set the random schedule seed when Hawk is built with random schedule debugging.

